  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday Night through Monday) \nIssued at 1052 PM CDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nAn upper low is expected to evolve off the West Coast tomorrow and\nwill make slow progress eastward into the CONUS through the end of\nthe week. An amplified downstream ridge will prevail over the\nPlains during the latter half of the week. Dry weather and\ncontinued above average temps can be expected. \n\nThe models take the majority of the energy from this initial system\nnorth toward away from our region and toward the northern Plains \nlate this week, with some energy hanging back over the Southwest. \nThe forecast area will remain under the influence of ridging at \nthe surface and aloft, so the onset of rain chances keeps getting \npushed back. Bottom line, rain chances through this forecast \nremain low at best and will continue to be until the second system\nin the Southwest finally comes east.\n\nLacy",
